# BOLT Phase 16 — real-CCTX detection evaluation (scenario_6)
# contribution C1-eval; closes gap G3 (circular '0% FPR') — non-circular evaluation
#
# ANTI-CIRCULARITY NOTE (the whole point of Phase 16):
#   thresholds/location-scale for EVERY detector are calibrated on the TRAIN split
#   (data/cctx/train.parquet, 100% benign). ALL metrics (ROC/PR/AUC/F1/phi/ARL) are
#   measured on the HELD-OUT TEST split (data/cctx/test.parquet), which is where the
#   incident rows live. train != test; the threshold-setting data is NEVER scored.
#   train rows=58146 (benign), test rows=24921 (benign + 382 incident).
#   sha256 verified: train=True test=True
#   positive labels: ['incident:nomad', 'incident:ronin']
#
# UNITS: the raw CCTX 'value' is the on-chain amount in token BASE UNITS with MIXED
#   per-token decimals (18-dec ETH-class next to 6-dec USDC / 8-dec WBTC) — NOT
#   cross-token comparable, so all detectors score value_usd (upstream per-tx USD
#   valuation, the one common denomination). Verified on the Ronin drain row:
#   1.736e23 base units = 173,600 ETH and value_usd = 539,884,276 USD.
# SCALE: heavy-tailed value scored as signed log-z (log10(value)-mu_log)/sigma_log,
#   mu_log=2.8902 sigma_log=1.0894 calibrated on TRAIN benign;
#   identical scale for the detector's value_z feature and the value baselines.
# runtime: 48.4s  (node-less; pure Python/data)
#
# PARAMETER SELECTION (V2 2.3 — train-only, non-circular):
#   SelectedParams: drift(δ)=0.25 threshold(λ)=4 cap=2
#   phi_train=0.00351 power_train=0.922 fpr_budget=0.01 grid_size=45
#   procedure: FPR-budget<=0.01 on TRAIN benign stream; power over TRAIN-only geometry family sigma=(1.0, 2.0) x events=(30, 90) (12 drains on TRAIN cadence; DISJOINT from the sigma=1.5/60-event eval point); grid 45 configs; seed 42
#   NOTE: the selected triple differs from the legacy hand-picked (δ,λ,cap)=(0.5, 8.0, 2.0) — the headline sequential-cpd φ/AUC below
#   SUPERSEDE the previous (legacy-triple) log/ledger values. Ablation deltas:
#   docs/bolt/ablations.md (Table 1 marks both configs).
#   Composite weights (0.5,0.3,0.2) and ALERT=3.0/CRITICAL=6.0 stay
#   dissertation-fixed (§11.2.3) — ablated in docs/bolt/ablations.md, never
#   train-selected; their FPR behaviour is characterised by scenario_4.
#
# GEOMETRY DISJOINTNESS (B2a): the (delta,lambda,cap) selection maximises power over a
#   TRAIN-only attack-geometry family sigma=(1.0, 2.0) x events=(30, 90)
#   (drains on the TRAIN cadence); the low-and-slow claim is evaluated at
#   sigma=1.5/60 events on the TEST cadence — a geometry in NEITHER
#   coordinate of the selection family, so the params were never tuned to the
#   exact attack they are scored against. The sigma sweep below shows the full
#   seq-vs-value trade including the crossover.
#
# SCORE SEMANTICS (B6): the sequential detector's per-row ROC/PR score below is the
#   INSTANTANEOUS Page-Hinkley statistic at each row. The previous headline used the
#   RUNNING MAX of that statistic — monotone non-decreasing along the stream, so its
#   AUC partly ranks rows by TIME-ORDER (later rows outrank earlier ones regardless
#   of content), an artifact for a per-row separability metric. Both are reported:
#     instantaneous (PRIMARY per-row score): AUC-ROC=0.9700 AUC-PR=0.3740
#     running-max  (ANNOTATED ARTIFACT):     AUC-ROC=0.9562 AUC-PR=0.5381
#   Change-point-native metrics (detection delay, ARL, precision at the matched
#   phi budget) are the PRIMARY metrics for this detector class and lead the log;
#   per-row ROC/PR is secondary either way.
#
# OPERATING POINTS (B4): every baseline's flag threshold is FPR-MATCHED on the
#   benign TRAIN stream to the same budget the sequential detector's selection uses
#   (phi_train <= 0.01); realized TEST phi is reported per row (train->test
#   drift means it can exceed the train budget — reported, not hidden). The old
#   'as-published/default' operating points (value-zscore at the q=0.999 fast-path
#   quantile, robust-MAD k=3.5, IsolationForest contamination='auto') appear ONLY in
#   the clearly-labelled secondary table.

============================================================================================================
PRIMARY METRICS (B6) — change-point-native: detection delay / run lengths / precision
     at the matched phi budget, on the HELD-OUT REAL TEST split
============================================================================================================
A streaming change-point detector is judged by WHEN it fires (delay after onset,
run length between false alarms) and WHAT its alarms are worth (precision at a
fixed benign-FPR budget) — not by per-row population AUC (secondary table below).

detector                      ARL0(s)    ARL1(s)  prec@op  phi(test)  target(train)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
sequential-cpd                371,868          0   0.5079     0.0025         <=0.01
value-zscore                   22,648          0   0.0366     0.0548         <=0.01
iforest-corrected               7,129          0   0.0113     0.1819         <=0.01
robust-mad                     26,350          0   0.0432     0.0460         <=0.01
xchainwatcher-rules      >=23,055,842          0   1.0000     0.0000 rule-based (n/a)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARL0 = mean run length between FALSE trips on benign TEST (seconds; '>=' = right-censored
       lower bound when the detector never false-trips, as Phase 12 reported).
ARL1 = mean time-to-detection (seconds) after the real Ronin incident onset on TEST.
       NOTE: a sequential-detector Ronin ARL1 of 0 s reflects the Ronin row tripping the
       fast path on its OWN event (its signed-log-z exceeds the train fast-path quantile) — a
       single-event catch IDENTICAL to a value threshold, NOT a sequential-accumulation
       result. The representative time-to-detection for the accumulating/low-and-slow
       regime is the NOMAD-onset ARL1 = 1,408 s (per-counterparty accumulation, the
       genuine sequential capability the detector is sold on).
prec@op = precision at the flag operating point (every operating point calibrated on
       TRAIN to the same benign-FPR budget 0.01 — B4; see calibration lines below).
phi  = realized benign false-positive rate at that operating point on HELD-OUT TEST.

Per-destination detection delay (sequential detector, real Nomad structuring
destinations — the distributional PRIMARY delay statement; full detail in 16.5):
  detected 14/16 destinations; mean finite delay = 1,792 s,
  bootstrap 95% CI [1,144, 2,536] s; never detected: 2 (reported, not dropped).

Operating-point calibration provenance (B4):
  sequential-cpd         (δ,λ,cap) train-selected under φ_train<=0.01; fast-path z=q0.999=3.414
  value-zscore           |log-z| > 2.873 (TRAIN q0.99, 1% budget)
  iforest-corrected      score > 0.6907 (TRAIN q0.99, 1% budget)
  robust-mad             robust-z > k=3.999 (TRAIN q0.99, 1% budget; as-published k=3.5 secondary)

