## Per-incident results (temporal holdout)
============================================================================================================
Protocol: for EACH incident, calibration = benign-only rows strictly before
onset - 1 h on the reassembled FULL timeline (train + test in true time order);
LogScale, the fast-path z (q=0.999) and the (delta, lambda, cap) selection are all
REFIT on that calibration only (no future information); the window
[onset, onset + 7 d] is then streamed in true order. Stronger than the single
time split: each incident gets its own no-future-information calibration.

  incident         detector             n_pos  recall          95% CI           method   prec  phi_win  n_calib
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  incident:nomad   sequential-cpd         380   0.163   [0.129,0.200]        bootstrap  1.000   0.0000    82575
  incident:nomad   value-zscore           380   0.029   [0.013,0.045]        bootstrap  0.846   0.0230    82575
  incident:nomad   xchainwatcher-rules    380   1.000   [1.000,1.000]        bootstrap  1.000   0.0000    82575
  incident:ronin   sequential-cpd           2   1.000   [0.158,1.000]  clopper-pearson  0.154   0.0031    65448
  incident:ronin   value-zscore             2   1.000   [0.158,1.000]  clopper-pearson  0.087   0.0058    65448
  incident:ronin   xchainwatcher-rules      2   1.000   [0.158,1.000]  clopper-pearson  1.000   0.0000    65448
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Leak check (asserted in main): every incident's calibration_max_ts < onset_ts:
  incident:nomad   onset=2022-08-01 21:32:31+00:00  calibration_max_ts=2022-08-01 20:30:31+00:00
  incident:ronin   onset=2022-03-23 13:29:09+00:00  calibration_max_ts=2022-03-23 12:29:00+00:00

READ THIS CORRECTLY (the honest shape this table exists to SHOW, not to improve):
the 382 pooled positives are really ~one Nomad event + one two-row Ronin event, so
pooled metrics are dominated by Nomad and the effective incident-level n is 2.
Ronin (n=2): ANY recall estimate carries a WIDE Clopper-Pearson CI — two rows prove
little on their own. Nomad: the sequential detector's per-row recall is LOW under
this stricter per-incident calibration (consistent with the pooled FN majority) —
